{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01NouPwByjtSBMtCZSbpd2qK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`ai-engineering/answers/05-007-shap-lime-model-interpretability.md`** covering:\n\n- **SHAP** — Shapley-value attribution (TreeSHAP for tree models, KernelSHAP model-agnostic), exact local accuracy + consistency guarantees\n- **LIME** — fast but high-variance local surrogate linear model; no consistency guarantee\n- **Transformers** — attention ≠ importance (Jain & Wallace 2019); Integrated Gradients via `transformer-interpret` is the theoretically-sound alternative\n- **Production example** — XGBoost credit model with TreeSHAP for FCRA adverse-action notices; SHAP Text masker for DistilBERT negation debugging\n- **Pitfalls** — attention-as-explanation mistake, LIME instability, local vs global conflation\n- **Cross-links** — hallucination detection (Q3), confidently-wrong RAG debugging (Q6), bias/fairness (Q14)\n\nNext up: **Q8 — Measure hallucination rate in production?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_read_input_tokens":67210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":333,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c506450-3731-4fc4-b9eb-d922430c70f2","uuid":"e7b27609-fbeb-434c-8d7c-a14223110bfd"}
